{"kind": "method", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/MissionZeroDriftScheduleTests.cs", "method": "LoopUnit_WithSchedule_IsNonOverlapping_Invariant", "line": 890, "verdict": "misleading", "category": "T3", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/GhostPlaybackLogic.WarpLoopPolicy.cs:247; flip UnitMemberOverlaps to OverlapCadenceSeconds > span -> red", "note": "Name claims a scheduled unit is BUILT non-overlapping, but the test constructs the LoopUnit itself with overlapCadence=max(span,MinInterval); the builder site is never reached."}
{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-mission-groups-006-01", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/MissionZeroDriftScheduleTests.cs", "line": 890, "method": "LoopUnit_WithSchedule_IsNonOverlapping_Invariant", "category": "T3", "severity": "Medium", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/MissionLoopUnitBuilder.cs:420; set minSpacing to 0 instead of cadence (drop the span floor) -> test stays green", "what_it_asserts": "That a hand-built LoopUnit whose overlapCadenceSeconds is max(span, schedule.MinIntervalSeconds) reports UnitMemberOverlaps false.", "why_weak": "The test replicates the builder's span-floor inline, so the production guarantee it names (MissionLoopUnitBuilder.cs:420 minSpacing = cadence >= span, and the OverlapCadenceSeconds it passes) is never exercised; removing that floor leaves the test green.", "proposed_action": "Rename to state what it pins (UnitMemberOverlaps on a schedule-carrying unit), and add a builder-level case that runs MissionLoopUnitBuilder for a scheduled mission and asserts the produced unit's OverlapCadenceSeconds >= span.", "effort": "M", "july_ref": "none"}
{"kind": "coverage", "sut": "MissionLoopUnitBuilder", "sut_file": "Source/Parsek/MissionLoopUnitBuilder.cs", "sut_line": 420, "case_kind": "integration", "proposed_name": "BuildLoopUnits_ScheduledMission_OverlapCadenceFlooredAtSpan", "sketch": "Build a drifting multi-constraint mission through MissionLoopUnitBuilder so TryBuildRelaunchSchedule attaches a schedule; assert the produced LoopUnit has RelaunchSchedule non-null and OverlapCadenceSeconds >= SpanEndUT - SpanStartUT, hence UnitMemberOverlaps false.", "guards": "A regression that drops the span floor on minSpacing / overlapCadence and lets a scheduled mission overlap itself in playback.", "risk": "playback"}
